<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valentinian II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">371–392</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valentinian II (371–392) was western Roman emperor from 375, proclaimed at the age of four after the death of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-i">Valentinian I</a>. Dominated by his mother Justina, then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> and finally by the Frankish general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arbogast">Arbogast</a>, he never ruled independently. He was found hanged at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> in 392, and Arbogast raised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenius">Eugenius</a> to the throne in his place.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentinian-ii.jpg" alt="Valentinian II" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brastite at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_emperor_Valentinian_II.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
